[claims]

## (root)
#c1[i5] ItsDangerous provides cryptographic signing helpers to safely pass data to untrusted environments and verify tokens have not been tampered with.
  > README.md::ItsDangerous #9862506eae8f
#c2[i4] ItsDangerous allows custom data serialization, automatic compression when needed, and automatic timestamp addition and verification during loading.
  > README.md::ItsDangerous #9862506eae8f
#c3[i2] The Pallets organization develops and maintains ItsDangerous and accepts donations at palletsprojects.com/donate.
  > README.md::Donate #d5eca4501200

## docs
#c4[i5] The documentation file docs/changes.rst includes the root CHANGES.rst file.
  > docs/changes.rst:4 #b0937da7f837
#c5[i5] ItsDangerous provides a Signer to sign bytes based on signing parameters, while a Serializer wraps a signer to serialize and sign other data types.
  > docs/concepts.rst:8-11 #8446375b6053
#c6[i4] Salts are combined with the secret key to derive unique keys that distinguish different contexts, and unlike secret keys, salts do not need to be random or private.
  > docs/concepts.rst:59-62 #16ea4b1b460d
#c7[i3] Serializers cannot load data dumped with a different salt, raising a BadSignature error when salt values mismatch.
  > docs/concepts.rst:83-84 #b93dd6a16c99
#c8[i4] When key rotation is configured by passing a list of secret keys ordered from oldest to newest, signing uses the newest key, while validation tries keys from newest to oldest.
  > docs/concepts.rst:116-119 #343f8b7f541a
#c9[i4] The default digest_method used by a signer as an intermediate hash step in HMAC generation is hashlib.sha1.
  > docs/concepts.rst:140-142 #f0ab46989cc2
#c10[i3] Configuring a signer with digest methods like hashlib.sha512 produces longer hashes, which increases token length in space-sensitive contexts like cookies and URLs.
  > docs/concepts.rst:152-154 #60ea180f0107
#c11[i4] The release and version configuration values are retrieved dynamically for 'itsdangerous' using get_version from pallets_sphinx_themes.
  > docs/conf.py:9 #6c76fe2f2cf3
#c12[i3] Sphinx documentation project metadata sets the project name to 'ItsDangerous' and copyright/author to 'Pallets'.
  > docs/conf.py:6-8 #9df9727c392f
#c13[i3] Autodoc settings configure class content to include both class docstrings and __init__, order members by source, put type hints in descriptions, and preserve default values.
  > docs/conf.py:21-24 #c8f7578f51a4
#c14[i3] The Sphinx HTML theme is set to 'flask' with index sidebar logos disabled.
  > docs/conf.py:35-36 #62923d51e83e
#c15[i2] Intersphinx maps Python documentation references to 'https://docs.python.org/3/'.
  > docs/conf.py:29-31 #d68e5d7fd11f
#c16[i3] The module `itsdangerous.encoding` provides encoding utilities including `base64_encode` and `base64_decode`.
  > docs/encoding.rst:1-8 #92aa2b623b31
#c17[i5] The module itsdangerous.exc documents exceptions including BadData, BadSignature, BadTimeSignature, SignatureExpired, BadHeader, and BadPayload.
  > docs/exceptions.rst:1-22 #a5862d4c7c89
#c18[i5] ItsDangerous allows cryptographically signing data using a secret key so that data sent to untrusted environments can be verified upon return.
  > docs/index.rst:14-16 #610b0ac928a6
#c19[i3] ItsDangerous can be installed and updated using pip with the command 'pip install -U itsdangerous'.
  > docs/index.rst:30 #77ecf647ba56
#c20[i3] Using signed user IDs in activation or unsubscribe URLs eliminates the need to generate and store one-time tokens in a database.
  > docs/index.rst:38-41 #53667b00144e
#c21[i3] Storing signed objects in cookies avoids storing sessions on the server and reduces database queries.
  > docs/index.rst:42-44 #adad5cdead64
#c22[i5] The documentation specifies the BSD-3-Clause License.
  > docs/license.rst:1 #9d684d32ff82
#c23[i4] The license text is included directly from the '../LICENSE.txt' file.
  > docs/license.rst:4 #3dbfb9101b84
